 - [2026-10-15] **The profile feature is built, on both sides, and tested.** Everything the previous note said was missing now exists. Member half: `PATCH /api/account/profile` (visibility, bio of at most 200 characters, alert-summary switch — origin check, session check, rate limit, upsert, an emptied bio stored as `NULL`, an unknown visibility refused), `POST`/`DELETE /api/account/profile/hidden` (hide a report from your own listing; ownership checked first, hiding twice is not an error, a deleted report answers 404), `/you/profile` (settings, badges with the reason and date of each grant, reports with a hide switch, anonymous ones flagged with nothing to hide) and `/u/<handle>` (a private profile answers 200 with a plain panel instead of 404ing; the owner and staff see the real page with a banner). Three rules are stated once in `src/lib/profile.ts`: a missing settings row means *open*; hiding a report removes it **from the listing only** — it stays on the map, keeps its confirmations and still counts in the record; and an anonymous report is never listed by name, its own author included. Staff half on `PATCH /api/admin/users`: `note` (append-only `member_notes`, never shown to the member), `grantBadge` (reason required and shown publicly, optional expiry, re-granting replaces the live grant, `desk` never hand-granted) and `revokeBadge` (clears the live grant, keeps the row so the record survives), each writing an audit row; the admin member page shows live grants with a Revoke button, the revoked history, a note box and the notes list. `src/lib/badges.ts` now sources "verified" from live grants — the explicit verification system its own comment promised — so a revoked or expired badge disappears on the next request.
 - [2026-10-15] How the feature was verified, since the tests are the deliverable as much as the code: a real PostgreSQL 16 server with the schema pushed from `src/db/schema.ts` and seeded by `src/db/seed.sql`, the SMTP capture server, and the real Next.js routes over HTTP. `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run lint` clean, `npm run build` succeeds with `/you/profile`, `/u/[handle]`, `/api/account/profile`, `/api/account/profile/hidden` and `/api/admin/users` in the route table (the first build attempts here failed only on `next/font` fetching Google Fonts, which this sandbox cannot reach — CI can — so the build was verified with the font loaders temporarily stubbed and the file restored, tree clean). `npm run test:local` 53/53 across all six suites, `npm run test:ui` 7/7, `npm test` 7/7, and the new `tests/profile.test.mjs` 9/9: defaults for a brand-new member, settings round-tripping onto the public page, everything the routes must refuse (junk visibility, a 400-character bio, a cross-site origin, a stranger's report, an id that is not an id), hiding and unhiding with proof the report is still on the map and still counted, what going private hides, and the staff side (a member cannot reach it, a badge needs a reason, re-granting replaces rather than stacks, revoking keeps the record, a note never reaches the member, the audit log carries `member.note`, `badge.grant` and `badge.revoke`). Three test bugs found and fixed on the way, each a real lesson about the product: both profile pages print a report's *title* rather than its street; JSX splits text around an interpolation, so `assert.match` on a sentence with a variable in it must stop before the variable; and two reports filed at the same place trip the app's own 180 m duplicate rule, so the hiding test files its pins on opposite sides of New Providence. The suites also needed `src/db/seed.sql` and a `MAIL_FROM` containing `nowbey.test`, both now part of the local stack.
 - [2026-10-15] Noted while running the suites: `tests/harness/env.mjs` refers to `tests/run-local.sh` for wiring the local stack (Postgres, a self-signed certificate, the SMTP catcher, `npm run dev`), but that script is not in the repository — the stack has to be assembled by hand. Worth committing, because the failure mode without it is confusing: a fresh database built only from `src/db/create-tables.sql` is missing columns that `schema.ts` has (the first full test run here failed 22 tests on `column "token_hash" does not exist`, all of them fixed by `npx drizzle-kit push` against a database created from the schema).
-
+- [2026-10-15] Security update (full report: `audit/2026-10-15_security/REPORT.md`, evidence in `evidence/`). Fixed: free self-granted paid plans in production (demo checkout now needs `ALLOW_DEMO_PLANS=true`, checkout answers "Plans open soon"); first-come claim of `ADMIN_HANDLES` handles (needs `ADMIN_EMAILS` to register and a confirmed email for rights); wildcard CORS; cross-site writes (proxy refuses foreign/`null` Origin on unsafe /api methods); per-instance rate limits (shared `rate_limits` table with in-memory fallback); weak synchronous password hashing (versioned async scrypt, legacy hashes upgraded at sign-in); invented gas prices from the gas cron (now a no-op; SQL deletes the rows); security headers (XFO, frame/base/object/form CSP in production). Found and fixed a pool-exhaustion bug in `src/db/index.ts` (lazy proxy called pg methods with the wrong `this`). App 1.2.2: server switch signs out instead of leaking the token, https-only except local addresses, Leaflet SRI, `allowBackup=false`. New tests: `tests/security-unit.test.mjs` (in `npm test`/CI), `tests/security.test.mjs` (in `test:local`), `npm run fuzz`. Original code: 1/14 security tests pass; fixed code: 14/14 on dev and production builds, 62/62 live, 7/7 UI, 22/22 unit, 0 findings in 17,832 fuzz requests. Owner steps: TODO_HUMAN §0a (rotate Vercel token leaked at `9e4eb47`, run `src/db/add-security-fixes.sql`, set `ADMIN_EMAILS`).
